// Nested `exists` where the OUTER binder's only positive restrictor lives
// INSIDE the inner `exists` body. Both `v` and `g` occur as positive
// predicate-field arguments of the same `Access` atom, so each is bound to a
// finite column of the Access relation — the formula is range-restricted
// (safe) by the range-restriction definition and its `∃x.φ` labeling rule
// (the inner `∃g` propagates `∅ → v` up, since that fact does not mention `g`).
//
// Regression guard for a validator-incompleteness bug: `collect_range_
// restricted` had no `Exists` arm, so it never descended into the nested
// `exists` and wrongly rejected `v` as "not range-restricted". Distinct from
// 1143, where the outer binder is restricted at its own conjunct level — here
// the ONLY restrictor of `v` is under the inner binder.
//
// Semantics: "some Access happened within the last hour" — permit Alert iff
// such an Access is in the past-hour window (mirrors 1142's window shape).
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (v: String). exists (g: String). formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Access"::request{ input.user: v, input.resource: g }
};
